# web-analytics — empty env templates (mirrors the `env:` list in module.manifest).
# The generator appends these (blank) to the project's .env.example section.
#
# OPTIONAL and strictly OPT-IN: with both left blank, the tracking snippet renders
# nothing and the site reports no analytics. Fill them in .env (never commit values)
# to turn analytics on. Privacy-first + self-hosted ONLY — these point at YOUR Umami
# instance (services/analytics), never Google Analytics or any third-party tracker.

# The self-hosted tracker URL — the SAME value for every site you host. With the
# platform analytics service up (./scripts/analytics.sh up) it is served by Caddy at:
#   https://analytics.<BASE_DOMAIN>/script.js
ANALYTICS_SCRIPT_URL=

# THIS site's "website id" — create the website in the Umami dashboard
# (https://analytics.<BASE_DOMAIN>) and copy its id here.
# TIP for hosting MANY sites: instead of this shared value you may set a PER-PROJECT
# override named <PREFIX>ANALYTICS_SITE_ID (the project's env prefix, e.g.
# ACME_ANALYTICS_SITE_ID) — the compose fragment prefers it and falls back to this one.
ANALYTICS_SITE_ID=
